<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lothair II of Italy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 926–950</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Lothair of Italy, Lothair of Arles</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-ii">Lothair II</a> was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-of-arles">Hugh of Arles</a>, who made him co-king in 931; he ruled alone from 947 until his early death in 950. He married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide">Adelaide</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-ii-of-burgundy">Rudolf II of Burgundy</a>, and after his death <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-ii-of-italy">Berengar of Ivrea</a> seized the throne. Adelaide's escape and marriage to Otto I in 951 drew the German king into Italy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lothair-ii-of-italy.jpg" alt="Lothair II of Italy" width="92" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: commons.wikimedia.org · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lothair_II_of_Italy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
